    {
      "chunkIndex": 2,
      "contentPreview": "A green test suite is not evidence that a GUARD works. The PermissionCoverageValidator shipped as a complete no-op and all 2561 solution tests passed. It surfaced only because the task required deliberately breaking a declaration and confirming the boot failed - it did not fail. Guards need a falsification pass: break the thing the guard exists to catch, confirm it fails and names the offender, then restore.",
